<title>SWEDEN: Sydkraft sees higher electricity prices.</title>
<headline>Sydkraft sees higher electricity prices.</headline>
<dateline>MALMO, Sweden 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish power company Sydkraft said  on Friday it expected the spot price for electricity to rise.</p>
<p>&quot;I think that the market has bottomed out,&quot; Sydkraft's acting chief  executive Lars Frithiof told Reuters in connection with a company  seminar.</p>
<p>Frithiof referred to a recent 1.5 percent upturn in demand for electricity.</p>
<p>He added that water levels currently are normal.</p>
<p>-- Kristina Zetterlund, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1005</p>
</text>
